1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:13,824
near_dart brings NEAR into Dart and Flutter.

2
00:00:13,824 --> 00:00:28,093
RPC, primitives, keys, transactions, and contracts.

3
00:00:28,093 --> 00:00:41,317
near_wallet_connect adds wallet UX for Flutter apps.

4
00:00:41,317 --> 00:00:53,078
Install near_dart and near_wallet_connect.

5
00:00:53,078 --> 00:01:05,048
Read balances, contract state, and app data.

6
00:01:05,048 --> 00:01:19,526
Build actions, sign, and send from Dart.

7
00:01:19,526 --> 00:01:35,336
NearCoffee is the SDK running as a real product.

8
00:01:35,336 --> 00:01:49,813
It shows production UX, not only unit tests.

9
00:01:49,813 --> 00:02:05,545
Intents do not replace wallets; they extend what apps can route.

10
00:02:05,545 --> 00:02:20,336
Quote, deposit instructions, status, and explorer data.

11
00:02:20,336 --> 00:02:32,907
AssetCatalog, QuoteBuilder, SwapController, ExplorerClient.

12
00:02:32,907 --> 00:02:47,385
0.1 wNEAR to USDC, live 1Click quote, no funds moved.

13
00:02:47,385 --> 00:03:00,818
The SDK avoids floating point mistakes.

14
00:03:00,818 --> 00:03:15,844
Discovery, quote, dry run, deposit guard, polling.

15
00:03:15,844 --> 00:03:28,415
Deposits become internal balances; signed intents authorize actions.

16
00:03:28,415 --> 00:03:42,840
Success, processing, refunded, failed, and expired are UI states.

17
00:03:42,840 --> 00:03:57,031
Connect wallet, quote intent, execute, poll, show receipt.

18
00:03:57,031 --> 00:04:12,762
near_dart is becoming a NEAR application SDK for Flutter.

19
00:04:12,762 --> 00:04:25,751
Install the SDK, run NearCoffee, and ship a real NEAR app.
